1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,470
AWS took 93 minutes to tell customers about an outage

2
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:06,470
The outage hit its US East region early on November 15

3
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:07,750
It began at 3:05 a.m

4
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:10,310
and lasted until 6:53 a.m

5
00:00:10,360 --> 00:00:13,750
THE ELEC says more than 10 major AWS services were affected

6
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:16,370
Users hit sign-up errors, authentication failures

7
00:00:16,420 --> 00:00:17,710
and connectivity issues

8
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:20,010
The main casualty was IAM Identity Center

9
00:00:20,060 --> 00:00:21,790
an enterprise login system

10
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:24,910
AWS engineers responded within minutes, the report says

11
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:27,630
But the first status page post came only after 93 minutes

12
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:30,530
The Register reports AWS questioned Downdetector's

13
00:00:30,580 --> 00:00:32,870
reliability instead of explaining the failure

14
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:34,750
The outage drew little attention, coming early

15
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:35,730
on a Sunday

16
00:00:35,780 --> 00:00:38,010
For Gulf firms on global clouds, outage communication

17
00:00:38,060 --> 00:00:38,890
is worth watching
